{"version":"2026.10.11-r25","id":"Q15427846","formula":"C₁₁H₉Br₂N₅O","hill":"C11H9Br2N5O","elements":["H","C","N","O","Br"],"composition":{"C":11.0,"H":9.0,"N":5.0,"O":1.0,"Br":2.0},"names":{"en":"Stevensine"},"descriptions":{"en":"Stevensine is a bromopyrrole alkaloid originally isolated from an unidentified Micronesian marine sponge, as well as the known sponge species, Pseudaxinyssa cantharella and Axinella corrugata. Total synthesis of stevensine has been achieved by Ying-zi Xu et al., and investigations into the biosynthetic origin has been explored by Paul Andrade et al. Understanding methods to synthesize stevensine and other similar compounds is an important step to accomplish, as marine sponges contain numerous biologically active metabolites that have been shown to function as anything from antitumor to antibacterial agents when tested for medicinal applications."},"fame":4,"pubchemCid":11003581,"mass":387.03,"charge":0,"smiles":"C1C=C(C2=C(C(=O)N1)NC(=C2Br)Br)C3=CN=C(N3)N","inchikey":"ZNIBKSGUBSYKLY-UHFFFAOYSA-N","iupac":"4-(2-amino-1H-imidazol-5-yl)-2,3-dibromo-6,7-dihydro-1H-pyrrolo[2,3-c]azepin-8-one","classes":[{"qid":"Q113145171","names":{"en":"type of chemical entity","ru":"тип химического объекта","uk":"тип хімічної сутності"}}],"structureInfo":{"kind":"molecule","source":"pubchem","ref":"11003581","atoms":28,"license":"PubChem (NIH), public data"},"structure":{"kind":"molecule","atoms":[{"x":0.761,"y":-2.673,"z":-0.943,"el":"Br"},{"x":-2.461,"y":-3.917,"z":0.22,"el":"Br"},{"x":-3.497,"y":1.553,"z":1.367,"el":"O"},{"x":-2.672,"y":-1.048,"z":0.45,"el":"N"},{"x":-2.083,"y":2.538,"z":-0.119,"el":"N"},{"x":2.318,"y":0.582,"z":0.849,"el":"N"},{"x":3.865,"y":-0.356,"z":-0.44,"el":"N"},{"x":4.417,"y":0.276,"z":1.824,"el":"N"},{"x":-0.736,"y":-0.208,"z":-0.233,"el":"C"},{"x":0.341,"y":0.705,"z":-0.53,"el":"C"},{"x":-1.998,"y":0.138,"z":0.236,"el":"C"},{"x":1.725,"y":0.34,"z":-0.35,"el":"C"},{"x":0.115,"y":1.958,"z":-0.984,"el":"C"},{"x":-1.235,"y":2.518,"z